<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred Dreyfus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a>–<a href="/years/1935">1935</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred Dreyfus was a French artillery officer from a Jewish Alsatian family. In 1894 he was falsely convicted of passing military secrets to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and sent to the penal colony on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devils-island">Devil's Island</a> in French Guiana. The campaign to clear him, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dreyfus-affair">Dreyfus Affair</a>, divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>; he was pardoned in 1899, fully exonerated in 1906 and returned to the army, serving in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus.jpg" alt="Alfred Dreyfus" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aron Gerschel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfred_Dreyfus_(1859-1935)_-_photo_originale.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
